hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16096","Abu Said, freedman of Banu Hashim, narrated to us, he said, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, from Abu Habbah al-Badri, he said, when Lam Yakun was revealed, Jibril, peace be upon him, said, O Muhammad, your Lord commands you to recite this chapter to Ubayy ibn Kab. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Ubayy, my Lord, mighty and majestic, commanded me to recite to you this chapter. So he wept and said, was I mentioned there. He said: Yes."
"16097","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Ammar ibn Abi Ammar, he said, I heard Abu Habbah al-Badri, he said, when Lam yakun alladhina kafaru of the People of the Book was revealed, to its end, Jibril, peace be upon him, said, O Messenger of Allah, your Lord commands you to recite it to Ubayy. And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ubayy: Jibril, peace be upon him, ordered me to recite to you this chapter. Ubayy said: And was I mentioned there, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Yes. He said, so Ubayy wept."
